{"sounds":{"intro":"High Valyrian is the ancient language of the Valyrian Freehold in Game of Thrones. It was invented by the linguist David J. Peterson for the series. It has no native speakers, but it has a full grammar and a few thousand words, and it is taught in a Duolingo course. This pool holds only words and phrases from the show and from the official course, with Peterson's spelling.","rows":[["ā / ē / ī / ō / ū","the vowel held long (the bar over it)","rytsas, valar"],["ȳ","like French \"u\" or German \"ü\"","sȳz"],["y","in the middle of a word, the same ü sound; at the start, like \"y\" in \"yes\"","nyke"],["r","rolled","rytsas"],["ñ","like \"ny\" in \"canyon\"","ñuhys"],["c","like \"k\"","dracarys"],["q","like \"k\", said further back in the throat","qurdon"],["gh","a gargling sound in the throat","morghulis"]],"notes":["This pool is small on purpose. Only words with a clear source are shown. The pronunciations are simple English-style guides, not exact.","The Duolingo course is the official place to learn more. Nothing here has been checked by the author of the language."]},"numbers":[],"greetings":[{"id":"greetings-and-sayings","title":"Greetings and sayings","items":[["hello","rytsas","RIT-sas"],["thank you","kirimvose","kee-REEM-vo-seh"],["no / not","daor","DAH-or"],["all men must die","valar morghulis","VAH-lar mor-GOO-lis"],["all men must serve","valar dohaeris","VAH-lar doh-HIGH-ris"],["dragonfire","dracarys","drah-KAH-rees"],["a girl has no name","riña dōre brōzi ēza","REE-nya DOH-reh BROH-zee EH-zah"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"questions-from-the-show","title":"Questions from the show","items":[["how much is this?","skorverdon kesy issa","skor-VER-don KEH-see IS-sah"],["is this Dornish wine?","kesy Dornīhor averilla issa","KEH-see dor-NEE-hor ah-veh-REEL-lah IS-sah"],["who holds the Iron Throne?","sparos Āegenkon Dēmalion dēmassis","SPAH-ros AY-geh-kon deh-MAH-lee-on deh-MAHS-sis"],["which way to the wedding?","skoriot dīnāzmot geron ilza","skor-ee-OT